{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17776 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Lobelanidin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to M19-MEL through multiple indirect routes. The first evidence links Lobelanidin to SF-188, which is a target of (1R,4aR,4bS,7R,10aS)-7-ethenyl-1,4a,7-trimethyl-3,4,4b,5,6,9,10,10a-octahydro-2H-phenanthrene-1-carboxylic acid, a compound that in turn targets M19-MEL. A second pathway connects Lobelanidin to HPAC, which is a target of Tupichinol A, also targeting M19-MEL. A third pathway links Lobelanidin to SF-188, which is a target of another compound that also targets M19-MEL. These findings suggest that Lobelanidin may act through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating a common downstream target, thereby contributing to the activation of M19-MEL. The evidence supports a potential role for Lobelanidin in the regulation of M19-MEL through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
